# Local runtime authorization gate

Full policy: [`docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md`](../../docs/guides/local-runtime-authorization.md)

## Canonical order (do not skip)

1. Inspect (read-only) → 2. Audit report → 3. Task gate (`ok`/`prossegue`) → 4. **Unit tests green** → 5. Infra gate (`ok infra`) **only if live proof needed** → 6. Live proof → 7. Commit-ready report → 8. Commit **only when owner explicitly asks**.

**Never** request infra before step 4 passes. **Never** commit before steps 4–6 succeed for the task scope.

## Three gates

| Gate | Trigger | After |
| ---- | ------- | ----- |
| Task | `ok` / `prossegue` | Inspect/plan accepted |
| Infra | `ok infra` / `autorizo infra` / `prossegue infra` | `./mvnw checkstyle:check test` BUILD SUCCESS |
| Commit | owner explicitly asks | Audit + unit (+ live if required) all green |

## Read-only without infra

Steps 1–2; `docker ps`; `docker compose config`; `lsof`; `colima status`; unit tests under task gate.

## Never without infra gate

`colima start`, `docker compose up`, `spring-boot:run`, `-Pintegration-tests`, live curl/smoke on agent-started stack, `docker compose down -v`.

## Infra brief must cite unit test success

Then: services, ports, coexistence, MacBook impact, stop plan → ask `ok infra`.

## Commit-ready ≠ commit

Report "pronto para commitar" with checklist; wait for explicit owner commit request.
